  "notes": "Touch kiosk for a hospital lobby built for legibility: Atkinson Hyperlegible, big 2px warm-grey bordered white panels on cream, very large hit targets. Route state color code: orange = current step and its highlighted map segment, teal = route, red = closures (x markers + 'Closed' pills), blue dot = you are here. Accessibility affordances are first-class (text size toggle, 4 languages incl. Vietnamese/Tagalog, step-free switch, slow pace default). Appointment-aware slack tile ('9 min to spare') recomputes when pace changes. 'Search for another place' opens (live, not in capture) a full-screen search with category chips, filter chips, 212-place grid and on-screen keyboard. Codebook lacks an entry for turn-by-turn directions / indoor wayfinding route lists (proposal filed: turn-by-turn-directions)."
